From 392d2a92438c2f278effce348ada3dfb83f76224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:51:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: reset inbound state only on restart

Commit 42c4cf5d4828 ("soc: qcom: smp2p: Add support for smp2p v2")
clears the last handled value of every inbound entry so that the values
a v2 remote writes after a restart are seen as changes. The commit
message scopes this to a detected restart, but the loop runs on every
interrupt whenever the SSR ack feature was negotiated.

Every notification from the remote then reports each set bit as a fresh
rising edge. On SM8550 the ADSP notifies several times a second while
its sensors stream, so the q6v5 ready and handover interrupts fire at
that rate and log "Handover signaled, but it already happened" each
time.

Only clear the inbound state when a restart is detected.

y700 (kernel y15): source armada-os/armada commit dac08dfe0a72
("fix(gyro): let the SoC reach deep sleep with gyro on", virtudude),
which adds packages/kernel/patches/0569-soc-qcom-smp2p-reset-inbound-state-only-on-restart.patch;
the file was cut byte for byte out of
https://github.com/armada-os/armada/commit/dac08dfe.patch (blob
ca3894883 matches). armada lists it as "upstream: not submitted". The
file has no Date and a placeholder author, kept as is; the date is
that armada commit's. Rebasing: none, the hunk applies to t52 at its
own line numbers (smp2p.c in t52 is v7.3's). Why: on the tablet the
smp2p-adsp interrupt runs at about 4.5/s with the screen on and the
"q6v5 ready" interrupt fires with every one of them (10-21 diagnostic
on 7.3-rc4, whose check_ssr() is v7.3's: 273 and 273 in 60 s), each
ADSP notification being replayed as a rising edge. v7.3's q6v5 masks
the handover interrupt after the first one, so the "already happened"
message does not show here. What is left is harmless: the replayed
ready edge is a nested call in smp2p's own irq thread to a handler
that only completes start_done, no extra wakeup. A correctness fix
carried with the next kernel build, not a power fix.

y700 patch file: 1053-soc-qcom-smp2p-reset-inbound-state-only-on-restart.patch

Fixes: 42c4cf5d4828 ("soc: qcom: smp2p: Add support for smp2p v2")
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
index af0ceeaf6..0d588688a 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -194,6 +194,9 @@ static bool qcom_smp2p_check_ssr(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
+	if (!restart)
+		return false;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
 		if (!entry->value)
 			continue;
-- 
